{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the control TAP parser repair at head 61b3c8d77bb522209aef384044f043686c03408c, tree e63b87c2, for request 0bcf9984 and review request af8e8648. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds seven paths to main e3e65a0b. `readTap` now reads a diagnostic through its own closing indentation, takes fields only at that indentation, and reads stdout only. An inconclusive result keeps the child's bytes.\n\n## Your four points\n\n1. The carried-over controls are enough. `git range-diff` shows 66e324d3 to 1366d582 and ed254389 to e314592d as identical, and the paths between the trees 65373cb5 and e712edbb are exactly the five landed paths of the abort repair, none of them on the parser's path. The gate reran the owner at the checkpoint. A rerun of the controls would add nothing here. The note also states this honestly.\n\n2. A nested closing line doesn't end the read early in the shapes I could make. I ran the real helper at this head on a scratch fixture, with real Node 26 failures:\n   - a multi-line assertion message holding `...` at depths 0, 2, 4 and 6, plus `---`, `not ok 7 - fake` and a `code:` line;\n   - the same text inside `deepEqual` values;\n   - the same text in a nested subtest.\n   All three classified as `AssertionError`. Node indents every value's lines below the diagnostic's own depth, which is why this holds, and a line at the diagnostic's own depth would need a value that Node doesn't emit. I tested Node 26.13.0 only.\n\n3. Keep the scripted case. It's small, it's labelled, and it fixes a boundary that real Node output doesn't reach: an unclosed diagnostic can't borrow the next record's fields.\n\n4. Retention can't change a conclusive result or a usage refusal. `preserveScratch` is set only inside `inconclusive`, and only once `scratch` exists. A conclusive path removes the directory as before. A usage refusal printed no retained path in my run, because it comes before `mkdtemp`. The exit codes don't change.\n\n## What I also checked\n\n- Unclosed diagnostics end at the next outer record and yield `Error (unknown)`, which can't count as an assertion. A diagnostic with no opening line reads as empty.\n- The request's done-when holds: the long Buffer case classifies as an assertion, and the old-ellipsis control fails on the old parser, with its nested ellipses and its own close at the lines that the note names. I read that from the note and verified the file digests, and I didn't rerun the control.\n- The gate at e314592d exits 0. Its `test.log` shows Node 98, Counting 56, Plain 3,203 with one skip and Native 889 with two skips. From there to this head, only the two notes and the manifest change.\n- The evidence verifies. All 16 manifest rows match, the manifest has digest e23b263b, the directory has 149 files, its `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with digest cfbc7c87, and no file is writable.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main e3e65a0b gives tree e63b87c2. `control.test.mjs` passes 3 of 3, `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `check-commit-messages` checks 3 with 0 flagged, `check-doc-links` on an export finds 775 links with 0 broken, and `git diff --check` is clean. The worktree stayed clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The note's reason for ignoring stderr is \"A test can write anything to stderr\", and a test can write anything to stdout too. With `--test-isolation=none`, a test that writes a well-formed record to stdout can still forge one. That's fine for a helper that runs our own tests, but this repair moves the boundary and doesn't close it. Don't describe it as forge-proof.\n2. A failure in a nested subtest reads as inconclusive. My fixture got \"4 tests ran before the change and 3 with it\", because the parent's `subtestsFailed` record is skipped and so leaves the count. This behavior predates this head. A control over a file with nested subtests will stop there, and it fails closed.\n3. Retained directories stay under the temp directory until someone removes them. The docs tell the reader to retain them with the evidence, and nothing cleans them up.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe change stays inside the helper, and the fixed Node list gains one owner. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nTooling only, with no product path. Retained files use mode 0600 in a fresh directory. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe parser gains a few lines for a real gain in correctness, and the owner tests the real CLI. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks hold. No deployment follows, and Workers stay on 112eff12 until J4 closes.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:866ecbc52d031ad9f9a58f1aceb474385c626333","binding":"assigned","head":"61b3c8d77bb522209aef384044f043686c03408c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b3bf39215e4a490247c0f11f7a0063ed7cd066bc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ad69910f30dd35e103eaecf1fd2d20138f174b19\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b3bf39215e4a490247c0f11f7a0063ed7cd066bc","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06cd20716ace3fec0e11115078984a5b2bdae664, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:656ae37239edc399710097036ea728f0c2c2cb3d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:852828295144681802a376d4f441300717648d06, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:866ecbc52d031ad9f9a58f1aceb474385c626333, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af8e86489ac02abf7789f4a0b95de7a7c7c2370c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b3bf39215e4a490247c0f11f7a0063ed7cd066bc, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d74a9d6e1bb2ec7c2c638ba5e8d4392993a1b836, git:sha1:589bca982736a23